The first commit attempt failed because another session moved HEAD (`cannot lock ref 'HEAD'`).
The plan commit then landed before the code commit. No file was lost.

### Mechanism

The select step reads the push file of each affected gated row. It sets `substitutions` to
`--substitutions=_RELEASE_COMMIT_SHA=<pushed commit>` when `_RELEASE_COMMIT_SHA` is the only
`REQUIRED_` default of the file (marketing). It sets an empty string otherwise (sales-advantage has
two more `REQUIRED_` defaults, so it stays an open limit). The table has no new field: B-21 pins the
key set. The select step text is still equal in both workflows (W-18c). A scratch repository has no
push file, so the step returns an empty string there. No cloudbuild file changed.

